{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-19778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨2,3,0⟩$ and $b=⟨6,4,0⟩.$ Find $a\\times b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-19778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot 0-4\\cdot 0)i-(2\\cdot 0-6\\cdot 0)j+(2\\cdot 4-6\\cdot 3)k \\\\  & =(0)i-(0)j+(8-18)k \\\\  & =⟨0,0,-10⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-19778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e194ab3d4125702e953d089d452fd51581b82daeddff4a28b792dce86831ac43"} {"question" "q-19778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-19778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-10,0,10⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,-10,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,0,-10⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,0,6⟩"] ["math" "⟨10,0,0⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-19778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,0,-10⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-77429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨2,0,-4⟩,$ $b=⟨-1,1,2x⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=2\\sqrt{5}.$ Find $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-77429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2x\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 2x\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0+4)i-(4x-4)j+(2-0)k \\\\  & =⟨4,-4x+4,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-4x+4)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+16{x}^{2}-32x+16+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-32x+36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-32x+36} & =2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-32x+36 & =20 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-32x+16 & =0 \\\\ 16({x}^{2}-2x+1) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+1 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x-1 & =0 \\\\ x & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-77429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e194ab3d4125702e953d089d452fd51581b82daeddff4a28b792dce86831ac43"} {"question" "q-77429" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-77429" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-1,4"] ["math" "x=-1,\\,2"] ["math" "x=1"] ["math" "x=2"] ["math" "x=\\pm 1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-77429" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-275278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨-2x,3,5⟩,$ $b=⟨2x,0,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{909}.$ Then, in **ascending order**,  the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-275278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2x & 3 & 5 \\\\ 2x & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-2x & 5 \\\\ 2x & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-2x & 3 \\\\ 2x & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3-0)i-(-2x-10x)j+(0-6x)k \\\\  & =⟨3,12x,-6x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(12x)^{2}+(-6x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+144{x}^{2}+36{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{180{x}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{909} \\\\ \\sqrt{180{x}^{2}+9} & =\\sqrt{909} \\\\ 180{x}^{2}+9 & =909 \\\\ 180{x}^{2} & =900 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-\\sqrt{5},$ $x=\\sqrt{5}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-275278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e194ab3d4125702e953d089d452fd51581b82daeddff4a28b792dce86831ac43"} {"question" "q-275278" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-275278" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\sqrt{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-275278" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-275278" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-278837" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=5i+2j-3k$ and $b=-2i+j+4k.$ Find $a\\times b.$\n\n$a\\times b=$\n\n{{field-1}}$\\,i\\,-\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,j\\,+\\,$\n\n{{field-3}}$\\,k$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-278837" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 4-(-3)\\cdot 1)i-(5\\cdot 4-(-3)\\cdot (-2))j+(5\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =(8+3)i-(20-6)j+(5+4)k \\\\  & =11\\,i-14\\,j+9\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-278837" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e194ab3d4125702e953d089d452fd51581b82daeddff4a28b792dce86831ac43"} {"question" "q-278837" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-278837" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-278837" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-278837" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-278837" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-278837" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-281976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $u=⟨\\sqrt{3},2,0⟩$ and $v=⟨1,0,-1⟩.$ Find $u\\times v.$\n\n$u\\times v=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-281976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot -1-0\\cdot 0)i-(\\sqrt{3}\\cdot -1-0\\cdot 1)j+(\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 1)k \\\\  & =-2i+\\sqrt{3}j-2k \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\sqrt{3},-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/state.json" "file_sha256" "d9ecaa5791b8a5137b064615da363a582611348f5c80bd65903c4c71a857b43d"} {"question" "q-281976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e194ab3d4125702e953d089d452fd51581b82daeddff4a28b792dce86831ac43"} {"question" "q-281976" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068395/